# Linear Regression Model Interpretation

## Coefficient

The coefficient shows how much the predicted target changes when the input feature increases by one unit.

In this project, Hours_Studied is the input feature and Marks is the target.

A positive coefficient means that predicted marks increase as study hours increase.

A negative coefficient would mean that predicted marks decrease as study hours increase.

## Intercept

The intercept is the predicted value of Marks when Hours_Studied is 0.

It represents the starting point of the regression line.

## Predictions

Predictions are the values generated by the trained linear regression model for new or test data.

The model uses the learned coefficient and intercept to estimate marks based on hours studied.

Predicted values can be compared with actual values to understand how accurately the model performs.

## Model Behavior

The model attempts to find a linear relationship between Hours_Studied and Marks.

In the sample dataset, marks generally increase as study hours increase, so the model learns a positive relationship.

Points closer to the regression line indicate smaller prediction errors.

MAE and MSE can be used to measure the difference between actual and predicted values.

Lower MAE and MSE values indicate smaller prediction errors.

## Conclusion

The linear regression model learns the relationship between study hours and marks from the training data. The coefficient describes the direction and size of the relationship, while predictions show how the trained model behaves on unseen data.
